    - for each arrow, plan 0-4 side-touch bounces along the diagonal
    - at each bounce, place a 1- or 3-pixel wall segment perpendicular to the flipped axis, 1 cell off the ray path; assign it a non-bg color
    - place arrow L-shape at ray origin (missing corner opposite to dir)
    - verify no cell overlaps between arrows, rays, and walls
    - input = arrows + walls on bg; output = input + ray cells painted
